    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "There was a time when the owners of shops and businesses in Chicago had to pay large sums of money to gangsters in return for 'protection'.",
      "translation": "曾经有一个时期，芝加哥的商店和企业主不得不向歹徒支付大笔金钱以换取“保护”。",
      "startTime": 15.2,
      "endTime": 26.32,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "protection",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "保护"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "If the money was not paid promptly, the gangsters would quickly put a man out of business by destroying his shop.",
      "translation": "如果不及时交钱，歹徒就会通过捣毁商店很快使那人破产。",
      "startTime": 26.33,
      "endTime": 35.45,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "promptly",
            "pos": "adv.",
            "meaning": "准时地，迅速地"
          },
          {
            "word": "destroying",
            "pos": "v.",
            "meaning": "破坏，捣毁"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Obtaining 'protection money' is not a modern crime.",
      "translation": "索取“保护费”并非现代的犯罪。",
      "startTime": 35.46,
      "endTime": 39.66,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "crime",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "犯罪"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "As long ago as the fourteenth century, an Englishman, Sir John Hawkwood, made the remarkable discovery that people would rather pay large sums of money than have their life work destroyed by gangsters.",
      "translation": "早在14世纪，一个名叫约翰·霍克伍德爵士的英国人就有一个非凡的发现：人们宁愿支付大笔金钱，也不愿让他们毕生的心血毁于歹徒之手。",
      "startTime": 39.67,
      "endTime": 56.5,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "remarkable",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "非凡的"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Six hundred years ago, Sir John Hawkwood arrived in Italy with a band of soldiers and settled near Florence.",
      "translation": "600年前，约翰·霍克伍德爵士率领一队士兵来到意大利，并在佛罗伦萨附近定居下来。",
      "startTime": 56.51,
      "endTime": 105.35,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "Florence",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "佛罗伦萨（意大利城市）"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "He soon made a name for himself and came to be known to the Italians as Giovanni Acuto.",
      "translation": "他很快就出了名，意大利人称他为乔凡尼·阿库托。",
